<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani cotton market shut for holiday.</title>
<headline>Pakistani cotton market shut for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's main private cotton market, the Karachi Cotton Association, was shut on Monday for a local religious holiday. It will reopen on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On Sunday, the Association's official daily rates closed at 2,405 rupees per maund (37.32 kg) for NIAB-78 variety, 2,597.50 for K-68 and 2,618.50 for MNH-93.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
